IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-disability-pension`
IMPORT `cp4-survivors-pension`

-- Tests of section 58, subsections (1) to (5) and (9). Every expected value is worked out by hand from
-- the text of section 58, as written beside the assertion. All amounts and indices are invented.

§ `Tests -- section 58 (subsections 1 to 5 and 9)`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- Portions, positionally: base, first additional, second additional.
`the contributor's portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` OF 400, 100, 200
`the survivor's own portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` OF 200, 50, 25
`the test series` MEANS LIST 100, 103, 106

§§ `Section 58(1.1) -- the flat rate benefit`

-- 1986: $91.06. 1987: the 1986 amount times 103/100 = 93.7918. 1988: that times 106/103 = 91.06 x 1.06 = 96.5236.
#ASSERT `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` 1986 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 91.06
#ASSERT `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` 1987 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 93.7918
#ASSERT `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` 1988 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 96.5236
#ASSERT `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` 1985 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` 1989 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Finding: for 1987 the disability pension's flat rate benefit (section 56(2)(b): 233.38 x 103/100 = 240.3814) and
-- the survivor's (91.06 x 103/100 = 93.7918) differ, because the two subsections start 1987 from different amounts.
#ASSERT `s 56(2) — the flat rate benefit of a disability pension` 1987 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 240.3814

§§ `Section 58(1)(a) -- under 65, no retirement pension, before 2019`

-- Survivor born 20 June 1975; the contributor died 15 March 2012. The survivor reaches 45 on 20 June 2020 and is
-- deemed to on 1 July 2020 (section 2(2)); March 2012 to July 2020 is 100 months. Flat rate benefit 100 plus 37.5%
-- of (400 + 100 + 200) = 100 + 262.5 = 362.5. No dependent children, not disabled: reduced by 100/120.
-- 362.5 x (1 - 100/120) = 362.5 / 6.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (362.5 DIVIDED BY 6)
-- A survivor with dependent children at the time of the death is not reduced: 362.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
-- A disabled survivor is not reduced: 362.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
-- A survivor already 45 or older at the death has no months under 45: 362.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
-- With dependent children at the death, ceasing to be a survivor with dependent children on 10 September 2018: 22 months
-- under 45 (September 2018 to July 2020); 362.5 x (1 - 22/120) = 362.5 x 98/120.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 9 10)) EQUALS JUST (362.5 TIMES 98 DIVIDED BY 120)
-- Both reductions add: 100 months at the death and 10 months on ceasing on 5 September 2019 (September 2019 to July 2020).
-- 110 months: 362.5 x 10/120.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 9 5)) EQUALS JUST (362.5 TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 120)
-- Exactly 120 months (death in July 2010): the whole amount is taken away, 0. 121 months (June 2010): more than the
-- whole, which the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2010 7 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 58(1)(a.1) and (b) -- after 2018, and 65 or over`

-- (a.1): no reduction after December 2018: 100 + 37.5% x 700 = 362.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(a.1) — the survivor's pension for a month after 2018 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` 100 `the contributor's portions` EQUALS 362.5
-- (b): 60% of (400 + 100 + 200) = 420.
#ASSERT `s 58(1)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the contributor's portions` EQUALS 420
-- Subsection (1) chooses: December 2018 is before 2019 (paragraph (a)); January 2019 is not (paragraph (a.1)).
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2018 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 `the contributor's portions` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2018 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (362.5 DIVIDED BY 6)
-- A survivor born 2 February 1950 is 65 in February 2015, deemed so from 1 March 2015: from March 2015 paragraph (b) governs
-- (420), in February 2015 the survivor is still under 65.
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 2 2) FALSE 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 420
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2015 2 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 2 2) FALSE 100 `the contributor's portions` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 362.5
-- Where a retirement pension is payable to the survivor, subsection (1) gives no amount: subsection (2) governs.
#ASSERT `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) TRUE 100 `the contributor's portions` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 58(3) to (3.6) -- the three portions of the contributor's retirement pension`

-- (3): multiplied from the month of the first listed event. Event in July 2012; ratio 1.1; amount 300.
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 7 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 330
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 330
-- Several events: the earliest governs.
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2013 1 1, YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 330
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2013 1 1, YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 300
-- No event at all: no multiplication.
#ASSERT `s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) EMPTY 1.1 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 58(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 80 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 88
#ASSERT `s 58(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 80 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `s 58(3.4) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 200 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 220
#ASSERT `s 58(3.4) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` 200 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2012 7 20) 1.1 EQUALS 200
-- (3.2): 8.33% x 1000 = 83.3 where no retirement pension was payable; times the ratio 1.2 where one was: 99.96.
#ASSERT `s 58(3.2) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.1)` FALSE 1000 1.2 EQUALS 83.3
#ASSERT `s 58(3.2) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.1)` TRUE 1000 1.2 EQUALS 99.96
-- (3.5): 33.33% x 1000 = 333.3; times 1.2: 399.96.
#ASSERT `s 58(3.5) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.4)` FALSE 1000 1.2 EQUALS 333.3
#ASSERT `s 58(3.5) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.4)` TRUE 1000 1.2 EQUALS 399.96
-- (3.3) and (3.6): section 51 refers to the year a benefit becomes payable, or to the year of death where none was payable.
#ASSERT `s 58(3.3) — the year to which section 51 refers for the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` TRUE 2005 2010 EQUALS 2005
#ASSERT `s 58(3.3) — the year to which section 51 refers for the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` FALSE 2005 2010 EQUALS 2010
#ASSERT `s 58(3.6) — the year to which section 51 refers for the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` TRUE 2005 2010 EQUALS 2005
#ASSERT `s 58(3.6) — the year to which section 51 refers for the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` FALSE 2005 2010 EQUALS 2010

§§ `Section 58(4) and (5) -- Pension Index limitation removed, retirement pension without regard to the plan's reductions`

-- Died in 1970 and the pension commences in 1990: the index calculated without the limitation (1.5) is used, not the limited one (1.2).
#ASSERT `s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` 1970 1990 1.2 1.5 EQUALS 1.5
-- Died in 1973 ("prior to 1974") and the pension commences in 1990: the unlimited index again.
#ASSERT `s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` 1973 1990 1.2 1.5 EQUALS 1.5
-- Died in 1974 (not prior to 1974): the ordinary index.
#ASSERT `s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` 1974 1990 1.2 1.5 EQUALS 1.2
-- Died in 1970 but the pension commences in 1973 (not "a year after 1973"): the ordinary index.
#ASSERT `s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` 1970 1973 1.2 1.5 EQUALS 1.2
-- Died in 1970 and the pension commences in 1974 (a year after 1973): the unlimited index.
#ASSERT `s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` 1970 1974 1.2 1.5 EQUALS 1.5
-- (5): a payable amount of 500 and 80 withheld by a provision of the plan that reduces pensions of those over 65: 580.
#ASSERT `s 58(5) — the monthly amount of the survivor's retirement pension to use in subsection (2)` 500 80 EQUALS 580
#ASSERT `s 58(5) — the monthly amount of the survivor's retirement pension to use in subsection (2)` 500 0 EQUALS 500

§§ `Section 58(2) -- where a retirement pension is also payable`

-- A benefit of 25% of 1/12 of 60000 is 25% x 5000 = 1250; adjusted by 1.1: 1375.
#ASSERT `cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` 60000 1 EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` 60000 1.1 EQUALS 1375
-- A share of 150 against the survivor's own portion of 200: 40% x 150 = 60 and 40% x 200 = 80, the lesser is 60: 150 - 60 = 90.
#ASSERT `cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` 150 200 EQUALS 90
-- A survivor's own portion of 100: 40% x 100 = 40 is lesser: 150 - 40 = 110.
#ASSERT `cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` 150 100 EQUALS 110
-- (a): flat rate 100, no post-retirement disability benefit; contributor's portions 400/100/200, survivor's own 200/50/25, benefit X = 1250.
--   (i): 100 + the lesser of (I) 150 - min(60, 80) = 90 and (II) 1250 - 200 = 1050: 100 + 90 = 190.
--   (ii): C = 37.5 and D = min(15, 20) = 15: 22.5.   (iii): C = 75, D = min(30, 10) = 10: 65.   Together 277.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 277.5
-- A post-retirement disability benefit of 150 is greater than the flat rate benefit 100: (i) becomes 150 + 90 = 240; total 327.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` 100 TRUE 150 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 327.5
-- A post-retirement disability benefit of 80 is less than the flat rate benefit: the flat rate benefit stays: 277.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` 100 TRUE 80 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 277.5
-- A benefit X of 250: (II) = 250 - 200 = 50 is the lesser of 90 and 50: (i) = 150; total 237.5.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 250 EQUALS 237.5
-- A benefit X of 150: (II) = 150 - 200 = -50 is the lesser of 90 and -50: (i) = 100 - 50 = 50; total 50 + 22.5 + 65 = 137.5. The text states no floor at zero (NOTES.md, fork F-t).
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 150 EQUALS 137.5
-- (b): flat 100 plus the lesser of 37.5% x 400 = 150 and (1250 - 200 = 1050): 250. With a benefit of 300: min(150, 100) = 100: 200.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences before 1998` 100 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences before 1998` 100 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 300 EQUALS 200
-- (c): (i) min(A - B, 1250 - 200) with A = 240, B = min(96, 80) = 80: 160; (ii) A = 60, B = min(24, 20) = 20: 40;
-- (iii) A = 120, B = min(48, 10) = 10: 110. Together 310.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(c) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65, was born after 1932 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 310
-- (d): min(60% x 400 = 240, 1250 - 200 = 1050) + 60% x 100 + 60% x 200 = 240 + 60 + 120 = 420. With a benefit of 300: min(240, 100) = 100: 280.
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(d) — the survivor's pension in any other case where a retirement pension is also payable` `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 EQUALS 420
#ASSERT `s 58(2)(d) — the survivor's pension in any other case where a retirement pension is also payable` `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 300 EQUALS 280

§§ `Section 58(2) -- which paragraph applies`

-- The survivor born 5 May 1940 reaches 65 in May 2005 (deemed 1 June 2005). Month January 2010: reached 65.
-- Born after 1932 and retirement pension commencing in 2005: paragraph (c) = 310.
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 310
-- Retirement pension commencing 31 December 1997 (not after): paragraph (d) = 420 (using the second benefit 1250).
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 420
-- Commencing 1 January 1998: paragraph (c).
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 310
-- Born 31 December 1932 (not after): paragraph (d). Born 1 January 1933: paragraph (c).
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1932 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 420
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1933 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 310
-- Under 65 (born 1960): paragraph (a) when the retirement pension commences after 1997, (b) when before 1998.
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 277.5
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1997 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS JUST 250
-- Not both pensions payable: subsection (2) gives no amount.
#ASSERT `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 `the contributor's portions` `the survivor's own portions` 1250 1250 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 58(9) -- when a survivor first becomes qualified`

-- First met the criteria of subsection 44(1) in March 2010: qualified from the month following, April 2010.
#ASSERT `s 58(9) — the month in which the survivor first becomes qualified to receive the survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 2010 3 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2010 4 1
#ASSERT `s 58(9) — the month in which the survivor first becomes qualified to receive the survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 2010 12 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 1
